  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Steal it on the heavy touch",
  "description": "An area of about 30 × 40 metres with a full-size goal and goalkeeper. The attackers stand in a short line at the far end, each with a ball. Defender X waits in the middle of the pitch.\n\nA dribbles straight at goal and takes on X. X must slow A down and go in to win the ball at the right moment – there is no help behind X. It counts as a won ball once X has it under control. After the attempt A becomes the new defender and X joins the back of the line.\n\nCompetition: each player defends, for example, three times in a row. Most balls won wins – and the attackers count their goals. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Close down quickly, but slow down in good time and get side-on."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Steer the attacker one way, ideally out wide and away from goal."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Wait for the moment: go in when the ball is furthest from the attacker's foot."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Get your whole body between the attacker and the ball – not just one foot."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
